y unusual rains in remote  areas of the arabian peninsula  swarms multiplied and moved northeast to  iran  pakistan and india and south to  war-ravaged yemen  and eastern africa they are areas where  tens of millions of people  are already facing the threat of hunger  east africa  you know is extremely vulnerable they've  had three years of droughts they have  this year now  floods and and and and heavy rains  um so you know they're already um kind  of  very sensitive to any additional shocks  that might occur  there's a swarm um earlier this year in  northern kenya  that was 60 kilometers long and 40  kilometers wide  the summer breeding season will see the  problem increase  the weather could determine if this  becomes a full-blown locust plague  so an upsurge is kind of regionally  based on you know what we're seeing now  in east africa  but you know a plague then would be  basically from from west africa all the  way across to to southwest asia  the united nations is raising funds to  spray millions of hectares with  pesticide  some indian authorities are using drones  as an alternative to kill the locusts  but the chemicals can harm the  environment and other insects  scientists in kenya are developing bio  pesticides  and even agents that confuse locusts  into eating each other  they are also advocating that people  start eating them too  we think it's something to promote so  that a lot more people should engage  in this in this practice rather than  shine away thinking that it is a  primitive  man's food poetic justice perhaps but  something that would barely make a dent  in this  enormous threat redmond shannon global  news london  a cat who disappeared 18 months ago in  victoria bc  is back with his family and has quite  the tale to tell  who is that  this is the moment blue was reunited  with the owens family  and seven-year-old hayden he was  discovered on july 2nd  17 kilometers away from home he hadn't  been spotted since december of 2018.  it took about four hours a few traps and  some motion sensor cameras but blue was  scooped up the next day  blue has lost a few pounds but he is  sure making up for it now with unlimited  treats  and cuddles as he gets used to his  surroundings  the cat always comes back and that is  global national for this saturday i'm  robin gill tonight your canada is out of  this world it's comet  neowise flying over abbotsford bc bright  and early this morning  hope to see you back here tomorrow  everyone good night  [Music]
 

